Subject: [PATCH 36/41] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20a=20finger=20drags=20in=20th?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20cells=20(SPEC=20=C2=A79.6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A program that names areas of its cells with `a=touch` gets a finger's
drag there as the mouse's primary button. A touch that begins on the
cells, outside every surface, goes to hotty-blitz's cells touch
(hotty_host_cells_touch) with whether the program reports the mouse's
buttons and whether the viewport is at the screen. In an area it is held
like a touch on a surface: a pan scrolls as before, and a drag or a tap
becomes reports Ghostty makes itself (Surface.mouseReport), in the
program's mode and encoding: the press where the touch began, moves with
the button held, the release where it lifts or, at a second finger, on
the last cell. The left button is held in Surface.mouse.click_state for
the drag, nothing is selected, and a press drops the selection, as a
reported press does. Shift is left out unless Ghostty would report a
press with it (mouse-shift-capture), since Shift and a press select. GTK
gives the touch no click: touch_hotty already keeps GestureClick off a
touch that hotty-blitz holds.

Upstream lines: 4 (2 in Surface.zig, mouseReport and mouseShiftCapture
made pub; 2 of comment in the GTK surface). The logic is in hotty.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
